(- csvsql.py  -  read CSV files from data/. Support: pick a subset of columns; keep rows where one column equals a value; sort by a column ascending with a stable order on ties. If a named column is missing, either raise ValueError or return no rows  -  pick one rule and keep it. Quoted fields that contain a comma are one cell. An empty body yields no rows.) Tj
